{
  "id": "seated_elbow_flexion",
  "version": 1,
  "nameKey": "exercise.seated_elbow_flexion",
  "notes": "PLACEHOLDER THRESHOLDS - NOT CLINICALLY VALIDATED. Front view: the forearm moves TOWARD the camera, so the 2D elbow angle is close to a step function (~180 while the hand is below the elbow, small once it is above). It is a reliable rep counter, NOT a range-of-motion measure - the demo hides the angle for this exercise. A side view would measure it properly but means turning the chair.",
